---
import CodeBlock from '../ui/CodeBlock.astro';
---

<div class="page">
  <div class="docs-meta">docs &#183; v1.0</div>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Documentation</h1>
  <p class="docs-desc">Spryteo converts raster images and icons into clean, animateable SVG. Install it, then reach for whichever surface fits your workflow &#8212; CLI, HTTP API, library, or MCP.</p>

  <h2 class="heading">Install</h2>
  <p class="para">Requires Node 18 or newer. Install globally for the CLI, or as a dependency for the library.</p>
  <CodeBlock html='<span style="color:var(--muted);">$</span> npm install -g spryteo<br><span style="color:var(--muted);"># or, as a project dependency</span><br><span style="color:var(--muted);">$</span> npm install spryteo' />

  <h2 class="heading">Quick start &#8212; CLI</h2>
  <p class="para">Point it at a raster file. It writes a grouped, animateable SVG next to the source.</p>
  <CodeBlock html='<span style="color:var(--muted);">$</span> spryteo ./icon.png <span style="color:var(--accent);">--groups</span> <span style="color:var(--accent);">--out</span> ./icon.svg<br><span style="color:var(--muted);">  traced 1 path &#183; 3 groups &#183; 2.1 kb &#8594; ./icon.svg</span>' />

  <h2 class="heading">HTTP API</h2>
  <p class="para">POST an image, get SVG back. The body is the raw file; the response is <code class="inline-code">image/svg+xml</code>.</p>
  <CodeBlock html='<span style="color:var(--muted);">$</span> curl <span style="color:var(--accent);">-X</span> POST https://api.spryteo.dev/v1/convert \<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style="color:var(--accent);">-H</span> "content-type: image/png" \<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style="color:var(--accent);">--data-binary</span> @icon.png' />

  <h2 class="heading">Library</h2>
  <p class="para">Import the async <code class="inline-code">convert()</code> function. It returns an SVG string plus the group map.</p>
  <CodeBlock html='<span style="color:var(--accent);">import</span> { convert } <span style="color:var(--accent);">from</span> <span style="color:var(--muted);">&#39;spryteo&#39;</span><br><br><span style="color:var(--accent);">const</span> { svg, groups } = <span style="color:var(--accent);">await</span> convert(buffer, {<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;groups: <span style="color:var(--accent);">true</span>,<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;simplify: <span style="color:var(--muted);">0.4</span>,<br>})' />

  <h2 class="heading">MCP server</h2>
  <p class="para">Register Spryteo as an MCP server and agents can convert icons in-conversation. Add this to your client config:</p>
  <CodeBlock html='{<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style="color:var(--muted);">&quot;mcpServers&quot;</span>: {<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style="color:var(--muted);">&quot;spryteo&quot;</span>: { <span style="color:var(--muted);">&quot;command&quot;</span>: <span style="color:var(--accent);">&quot;spryteo-mcp&quot;</span> }<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;}<br>}' />

  <div class="docs-footer">
    <span class="docs-footer-text">Full reference lives in the</span>
    <a href="https://github.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="docs-footer-link">GitHub README &#8594;</a>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  .page {
    max-width: 820px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 64px 32px 96px;
  }
  .docs-meta {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }
  .docs-title {
    font-size: 44px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 0 0 16px;
  }
  .docs-desc {
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin: 0 0 48px;
  }
  .heading {
    font-size: 24px;
    font-weight: 500;
    margin: 0 0 12px;
    scroll-margin-top: 90px;
  }
  .para {
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin: 0 0 16px;
  }
  .inline-code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .docs-footer {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 28px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
  }
  .docs-footer-text {
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .docs-footer-link {
    font-size: 15px;
  }
</style>
